graph TB
  B["BINARY SEARCH TREE: a sorted sequence stored as shape<br/>for every node, every key in its left subtree is smaller and every key in its right subtree is larger"]
  B --> P["THE PROPERTY IS THE ORDER<br/>nothing is sorted during insertion, the shape carries the order alone<br/>the in-order walk of the sample tree returns 20 30 35 40 50 60 70 80: sorted, and that is the check"]
  B --> S["SEARCH: one comparison per node on the path<br/>search(50) 1 comparison, the root<br/>search(35) 4 comparisons<br/>search(10) 3 comparisons, reached a null pointer so the key is absent<br/>8 present keys cost 21 comparisons in total, 2.62 on average<br/>8 absent keys cost 24 comparisons, 3.00 on average"]
  B --> D["DELETE IS THREE CASES<br/>case 1, a leaf: unlink it, the rest of the tree is untouched<br/>case 2, one child: the child takes the place of the removed node<br/>case 3, two children: the in-order successor takes the key, then the successor is deleted from the right subtree, where it is case 1 or case 2 again"]
  D --> D2["THE SUCCESSOR IS THE LEFTMOST NODE OF THE RIGHT SUBTREE<br/>successor(50) = 60, the smallest key larger than 50<br/>copying that key up keeps everything left smaller and everything right larger<br/>after remove(50): 20 30 35 40 60 70 80, still sorted"]
  B --> H["HEIGHT IS THE COST, AND THE INSERT ORDER DECIDES IT<br/>the same 31 keys: sorted insert order gives height 31, median order gives height 5<br/>search(31) costs 31 comparisons in the chain and 5 in the balanced tree<br/>all 31 keys cost 496 comparisons against 129, so 3.84x for identical data: O(n) against O(log n)"]
